Correct. If you get an early wish, and if you want to spend it
on an artifact weapon, you'll have better chances if there are
not yet too many already existing.

The prayer timeout thing (and any luck issue) can be easily
fixed by sacrificing a few more corpses after you've received
your artifact. To quickly increase your luck throw identified
gems at a coaligned unicorn.

You're asking for reasons why to sacrifice at all...
You increase your early games chances to survive if you have an
artifact weapon.
Wishes are rare (or risky) early in the early game, an altar
seems much more common to encounter, IME.
There are many necessary things to have - and if you don't have
got them to wish for them - than to wish for an artifact weapon;
since you can get artifacts from sacrificing why wish for one,
spend the wishes on the essentials and get the artifact weapons
"for free".
There are many good artifacts that you can get from sacrifices,
not only the Magicbane.
There are differences in the quality of the various artifacts
but having any of them is mostly better than not having on at
all.

